{
  "id": "android_studio",
  "name": "Android Studio",
  "kind": "app",
  "category": "Development",
  "match": {
    "windows_exe": [
      "studio64.exe"
    ],
    "macos_bundle": [
      "com.google.android.studio"
    ],
    "window_title": []
  },
  "sources": [
    "https://developer.android.com/studio/intro/keyboard-shortcuts"
  ],
  "note": "From the Android Developers \"Keyboard shortcuts\" reference for Android Studio (default keymap), Windows/Linux and macOS columns; Linux equals Windows so no linux value is stored. The Layout Editor and Navigation Editor sections keep their name as the context and Debug keeps \"Debug\"; the other headings are groupings, so their context is empty. Where Google lists two bindings for one command the first is kept, except for slash-named commands (\"Zoom in/out\", \"Collapse/expand current code block\", \"Collapse/expand all code blocks\", \"Indent/unindent lines\", \"Next/previous highlighted error\"), which are split into the two commands they name. Omitted because the chord grammar cannot express them: \"Search everything (including code and menus)\" (press Shift twice), \"Pan\" (hold Space and drag), \"Select multiple components\" and \"Select multiple destinations\" (Shift-click / Ctrl-click). Android Studio is built on IntelliJ IDEA, so many of these also appear in the IntelliJ entry; this file follows Google's own published list.",
